 in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nRecent burn scars will also be especially susceptible and these\ninclude the Lee and Elk RX, Gold Mountain and Elk, Ferris, and\nBabylon burn scars to name a few.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoonal moisture will remain across the area through Monday\nevening and will support thunderstorms and showers with heavy\nrainfall across the watch area. Several rounds of heavier rain\nare expected increasing the chance for flash flooding especially\nin our more susceptible areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Central Yampa River Basin; Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley; Debeque to Silt Corridor; Central Colorado River Basin; Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre River Basin; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops; Upper Gunnison River Valley; Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Southeast Utah; Tavaputs Plateau; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-30T23:51:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 302351 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 551 PM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Multiple rounds of showers and storms are expected today, especially along and north of I-70. - Another wet day is on tap tomorrow as well, with higher coverage of precipitation across southeast Utah and southwest Colorado. - Flash flooding is possible thr","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-30T20:47:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Multiple rounds of showers are expected between now and Monday evening. Heavy rain, gusty outflow winds, and lightning will be the biggest concerns. Temperatures drop thanks to increased cloud cover and precipitation. Fire weather concerns remain minimal. A downturn in precip is possible for Tuesday and beyond. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS.","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cbl01","station_name":"Carbondale","distance_km":25.9,"soil_temp_5cm_f":61.61,"soil_temp_15cm_f":61.83,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":18.85,"wind_speed_mph":2.57,"air_temp_f":58.57,"relative_humidity":0.898,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/cbl01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KASE","distance_km":20.4,"raw_metar":"METAR KASE 310053Z 16005KT 10SM BKN080 BKN120 16/08 A3034 RMK AO2 SLP170 T01610078","temp_f":61,"wind_dir":160,"wind_kt":5,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"BKN","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1027.5,"observed":1788137580,"raw_taf":"TAF KASE 302335Z 3100/3124 18008KT P6SM SCT090 BKN100 PROB30 3100/3105 VRB15G30KT 4SM -TSRA BKN090CB FM311600 36007KT P6SM SCT070 BKN100 PROB30 3116/3122 VRB15G30KT 4SM -TSRA BKN090CB FM312200 12006KT P6SM OVC100 PROB30 3122/3124 VRB15G30KT 4SM -TSRA BKN090CB","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KASE&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":29,"category":"Good","parameter":"O3","reporting_area":"Aspen","observed":"2026-08-30 18","by_parameter":{"O3":{"aqi":29,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Aspen","observed":"2026-08-30 18"},"PM2.5":{"aqi":8,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Aspen","observed":"2026-08-30 18"},"PM10":{"aqi":4,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Aspen","observed":"